# Commit messages

Always write Git commit messages in **English**, even when the conversation or UI copy is in French.

- Focus on **why**, not a file-by-file dump
- Use the imperative mood: `Add`, `Fix`, `Update`
- Keep the subject to one line; add a body only when it clarifies intent

```text
# BAD
Ajouter la gestion locale des prêts de matériel.

# GOOD
Add local equipment loan tracking.

Persist add, edit, and delete of loans in the browser until auth and a database are in place.
```
